  "notes": "Still on many 787-8s, 777s and A320-family aircraft not yet repainted in 2025-2026 (Commons photos from 2025). Drawn from the 787-8; titles placed for the 787's longer fuselage, so on a narrow-body they sit a little further forward. Belly seen only edge-on from the side: the red is taken to run under, as the sides show, not confirmed from below. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the Devanagari title is given the English one's length (0.15; low: the left-side photo is at night); the belly's and the tail sweep's edges are curves (smooth).",
  "history": "Introduced 2007 with the Air India / Indian Airlines merger (the Konark wheel and the 'flying swan' heritage); superseded from 2023 by the Vista scheme (standard), repaint ongoing."
